{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Upgrade to 100/125cc the type of motorbike pre-Feb 2001 full car drivers can use",
        "additional_details": "This petition is seeking to allow people of my age and older who have ridden bikes up to 125cc many years ago to ride such bikes without a CBT or leaner lates. We want the law to increase it to at least a 100 or 125cc, as we believe this would make the roads safer. On 50cc bikes you can inadvertently create a rolling road block at 28mph, which can be dangerous if you ride on a dual carriageway, or a dangerous road.",
        "background": "I would like the Government to change the law that allows people who passed the full car license before 1 February 2001 to ride a moped up to 50cc without a CBT or learner plates. I believe this law is a waste of time & still very dangerous on today's roads & should be increased to at least 100cc.",
